    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What counts",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Each bar is a mean over the runs of this workflow that **ended in the range**, succeeded or called off, as the pick says: a run still\ngoing, or stopped at a gate nobody answered, is not counted yet. The numbers are the ones a run's page shows in its Timeline, handed over\nonce when the run ends (the `run.timeline` spans), so a range holding one run shows that run.\n\n- **Queued**, **Ran** and **Cost a session** are per session: a step's row is its session, the row under it its check. A step\n  whose every try ran a session of its own spent as many times its bar as **Tries a run** says.\n- **A step a person answered** ran one session: when it signs off blocked and is answered, the answer is a try more and a turn of\n  the same session. Its **Ran** and its cost are that session's, every turn of it, once; **Tries a run** counts each answer.\n- **A round's wall** is from the first filing of a round of a loop to its last end: its sessions, its checks and its queues.\n- **A run** sets its wall time beside what of it was waiting: in the queue, in its checks, at its gates for a person, and for a\n  person's answer (`waiting: answer`): from a turn that signed off blocked to the spawn of the turn the answer started, the pass\n  that heard it and its wait for a slot included. Work sent back from a gate with words is in neither wait.\n\nTempo answers seven days back, and a run is counted at the moment the daemon read it over, not when it ended. A run already counted\nkeeps the numbers it sent: none is sent again, so a run counted before a number was added has none of it."
      }
